      "summary": ": Sunday 9/8 We are Open today with 10cm of overnight freshies! It is still snowing with some wind affected drifts across the mountain. It is forecasted for more snow showers throughout the day and is likely to be cloudy so your low vis goggles will be recommended! There may be some delays on lifts and terrain as our teams work through some mitigation work and get the lifts spinning. Main Basin lifts will aim to be running from 08:30am with Captains, T-Bar to follow. Soho and Willows will be Closed for the day as visibility has not improved. Road Status: Chains on 2WD from Valley View --- earners Slope Open Main Basin Open Captains Open Soho Closed Little Willows Closed Big Willows Closed Ski Touring Access Closed Mt Cardrona Closed Arcadia Chutes Open Summit Closed",
